K1  ONE NR COMPONENT: what a first-order transition releases depends on where it happens
==============================================================================================================
    d/dn [n Delta(n)] - (V'(n) - mu_c) = 0,  mu_c = (V(n2) - V(n1))/(n2 - n1): zero only where V' = mu_c
    V = n^2 - 1.5 n^3 + 0.6 n^4: spinodals 0.289-0.961, coexisting phases n1 = 0.043, n2 = 1.207
    released per particle, Delta(n) = (V - V_hull)/n, across the unstable range: 0.1057, 0.1244, 0.1243, 0.1100, 0.0865, 0.0588, 0.0318
    relativistic branches at one charge density: phi_b^2/phi_a^2 = omega_a/omega_b (identity residual 0); with both omegas within 1e-05 of m the amplitudes agree to 1.0e-05: one branch
  [PASS] K1 one NR component has no universal latent heat: the release per particle follows V' - mu_c and varies by > 2x across the unstable range, with a dense phase among the products; NR relativistic branches coincide
         measured: identity residual 0; Delta spread 3.9x; branch identity 0
         reading:  a universal kick needs two internal states, not one component's phase change

